# Gemini API REST Specification for Rust HTTP Client

## Endpoint URL
```
POST https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{model}:generateContent?key={API_KEY}
```

The API key is passed as a query parameter, not in headers.

## Request Body Structure

```json
{
  "contents": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "parts": [
        {"text": "Your prompt here"},
        {"inline_data": {"mime_type": "image/jpeg", "data": "base64_string"}}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "systemInstruction": {
    "parts": [{"text": "System prompt text"}]
  },
  "tools": [
    {
      "functionDeclarations": [
        {
          "name": "function_name",
          "description": "What it does",
          "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "param_name": {"type": "string", "description": "..."}
            },
            "required": ["param_name"]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "generationConfig": {
    "temperature": 1.0,
    "maxOutputTokens": 2048,
    "topP": 0.95,
    "topK": 40,
    "stopSequences": ["STOP"]
  },
  "safetySettings": [
    {
      "category": "HARM_CATEGORY_HATE_SPEECH",
      "threshold": "BLOCK_MEDIUM_AND_ABOVE"
    }
  ]
}
```

**Key field names (exact casing):**
- `contents` - array of Content objects
- `role` - string: `"user"` or `"model"`
- `parts` - array of Part objects
- `systemInstruction` - Content object
- `tools` - array of Tool objects
- `functionDeclarations` - array of FunctionDeclaration objects
- `parameters` - Schema object (uses `type`, `properties`, `required`)
- `generationConfig` - GenerationConfig object

## Response Body Structure

```json
{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "content": {
        "role": "model",
        "parts": [
          {"text": "Response text"},
          {
            "functionCall": {
              "name": "function_name",
              "args": {
                "param_name": "value"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "finishReason": "STOP",
      "safetyRatings": [
        {
          "category": "HARM_CATEGORY_HATE_SPEECH",
          "probability": "NEGLIGIBLE"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "usageMetadata": {
    "promptTokenCount": 10,
    "cachedContentTokenCount": 0,
    "candidatesTokenCount": 50,
    "totalTokenCount": 60
  },
  "modelVersion": "gemini-3.7-flash"
}
```

**Key field names (exact casing):**
- `candidates` - array of Candidate objects
- `content` - Content object
- `parts` - array of Part objects
- `functionCall` - FunctionCall object with `name` and `args` (args is a map/object)
- `finishReason` - enum string
- `usageMetadata` - UsageMetadata object
- `promptTokenCount`, `candidatesTokenCount`, `totalTokenCount` - integers

## Sending Function Results Back

After a `functionCall` is received, send the result in a new request:

```json
{
  "contents": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "parts": [{"text": "Initial prompt"}]
    },
    {
      "role": "model",
      "parts": [
        {
          "functionCall": {
            "name": "function_name",
            "args": {"param": "value"}
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "parts": [
        {
          "functionResult": {
            "name": "function_name",
            "response": {"result_key": "result_value"}
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Role sequence:** user → model → user (with functionResult part)

## Streaming Endpoint

For streamed responses, append `?alt=sse` to the URL and handle Server-Sent Events with identical request/response JSON structures.

