//! The real agent: reasoning -> hypothesis (optionally grounded by a fast
//! static scan) -> empirical tool call (`shift_test`) -> verification ->
//! verdict, with a targeted retry when the model's read of the evidence
//! disagrees with the empirically-justified two-signal rule
//! (`verify::audit`) -- see `problem.md` §03 step 4 ("If inconclusive, it
//! explores an alternative hypothesis").
//!
//! Two tools are available: `static_scan` (a fast, free, deterministic AST
//! pass, `static_checks::scan`) and `shift_test` (the real empirical
//! backtest rerun). `static_scan` is optional -- a hint for hypothesis
//! formation, not proof either way. `shift_test` is the one thing a verdict
//! actually has to be grounded in; the loop below nudges toward it and
//! ultimately falls back to running it directly if the model never does.

